{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/976433-what-kind-of-signs-would-humans-notice-when-vampires-go-to-war-with-each-other","id":976433,"title":"What kind of signs would humans notice when vampires go to war with each other?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-26T02:49:40-07:00","id":976433,"title":"What kind of signs would humans notice when vampires go to war with each other?","content":"I wanted to know from a human perspective what kind of signs would they notice in there city when vampires go to war with each other. For example factions of the invictus ?<br /> <br /> what kind of head lines would there be and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T03:02:29-07:00","id":976438,"title":"","content":"Praxis usually frowns upon open destruction of your fellow kindred, to say the least about doing such on a massive scale as warfare entails. Is it a hot war? Then the signs should be apparent. Mayhem, chaos, etc.<br /> <br /> A cold war, on the other hand, got sleeper agents working without their very knowing, spawning bizarre &quot;Florida Man&quot; headlines, with each occurrence furthering the plot of one elder or the other. Hunters would be smart in checking up on such victims of vampiric mind-games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T04:34:23-07:00","id":976462,"title":"","content":"I'd say it depends on the number of vampires involved, their willingness to involve innocents and/or keep a low profile so that hunters don't start popping up, and their power obviously.<br /> <br /> It could very well look like your average gang wars, except with fewer corpses and more pieces of clothe full of of ash. Well, fewer corpses that you would expect, cause you might find some other corpses in seemingly unrelated places, most of them lacking a lot of blood for some reason. Blood becomes an important resource and when you need a lot to heal and fight, you can't be as careful. There would probably be more feeding accidents : dead people, people reporting being assaulted and bitten, maybe getting sick left and right (from vampires who don't take time anymore to check on their victim's health history and become carriers). I'd imagine that's if we're talking about generally low level vampires who are somewhat trying to preserve their humanity.<br /> <br /> Some vampires could be willing to start enslaving mortals left and right to build themselves a small army and this is where things could start getting really nasty. The gang war involving unknown groups of like 50 people now involves whole known gangs. Then, someone has the smart idea of putting a blood bond on the chief of police, the mayor and so on. You suddenly have a huge number of random police brutality and a big search for a number of drug stashes (rival vampire havens) during the day. That doesn't seem like a good recipe for keeping one's humanity, though, so hard to say how long that would last until the vampires responsible for this to become a draugr, which, if it is discovered (which is usually not too hard), might lead their allies to turn on them.<br /> <br /> Also, a war is the best occasion to slip in the occasional diablerie, there's another downward spiral.<br /> <br /> Lastly, the war being visible might be a good thing. Pushing the rival side to more and more extreme actions is a good way to get hunters to target them. Let them fight it out, lay low for a month or two and become the default new ruling faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T07:40:11-07:00","id":976512,"title":"","content":"That really depends on whether or not vampires care to advertise their presence to the collective human race. If two factions have reached a point where they've decided the other side has to be a pile of ash, the victors will be whichever side comes out to the government and vilifies the other side to humans first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T10:19:43-07:00","id":976599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/976433-what-kind-of-signs-would-humans-notice-when-vampires-go-to-war-with-each-other#post976433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to know from a human perspective what kind of signs would they notice in there city when vampires go to war with each other. For example factions of the invictus ?<br /> <br /> what kind of head lines would there be and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually &quot;hot war&quot;? (Actual attacks intending to result in final death) <a href=\"http://www.latimes.com/local/lanow/la-me-ln-man-arrested-starting-cedar-fire-20160929-snap-story.html\" target=\"_blank\">Wild-Fires</a>, <a href=\"http://komonews.com/news/local/seattle-housing-authority-helping-residents-displaced-by-west-seattle-apartment-fire\" target=\"_blank\">Apartment Fires</a>, <a href=\"http://www.pressherald.com/2016/09/21/12-charlotte-officers-injured-in-protests-after-police-fatally-shoot-black-man/\" target=\"_blank\">Riots involving arson/violent police response</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_nightclub_fires\" target=\"_blank\">any type of arson really</a>, <a href=\"http://www.buffalonews.com/city-region/emergency-demolition-ordered-friday-on-crumbling-building-on-west-ferry-street-20160624\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Emergency&quot; demolitions/excavations of &quot;vacant&quot; buildings/lots</a>. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/September_11_attacks\" target=\"_blank\">Day-time haven destruction</a> is the most devastating assaults on a vampire possible.<br /> <br /> Warm conflict? (Assaults meant to undermine infrastructure of another vampire) Gang violence, police cracking down on crime(specific or general), gentrification, crime-waves, cult or anti-cult activity, protesting, laws discriminating against certain areas or portions of the populace, and environmental land appropriation by the government.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-29-2016, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T20:20:21-07:00","id":976909,"title":"","content":"Its more of a shadow war with some hot spots. Right now the Invictus vs the circle of crone and they both are strong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T00:39:10-07:00","id":977045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/976433-what-kind-of-signs-would-humans-notice-when-vampires-go-to-war-with-each-other?p=976909#post976909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its more of a shadow war with some hot spots. Right now the Invictus vs the circle of crone and they both are strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Economic downturn as small businesses collapse, higher rates of murder (or at least death as murders can be disguised as natural causes / suicide / missing / etc.), sporadic vandalism and property damage. Basically all the symptoms of vampires sabotaging each others assets whether they be financial, property or people. General instability as people fight over control of tactical assets too - scandals deposing chief of police in favour of a new one every other month. Also people trying to build up new assets - a particularly cultish martial arts school for example (the sensai is a ghoul), a new firm of bouncers muscling in. A Cold War is about out-threatening your enemy. So look for instability in society, rapid transitions and a general lack of co-operation (e.g. you'd expect politician X and politician Y to find common ground and share information, but they don't because they're controlled by rival vampires).<br /> <br /> When the war gets hot, you can turn the above up a few degrees as power shifts are faster, businesses implode in scandals and the common people will probably get a general feeling that the entire society is hopelessly corrupt and messed up. You list Shadow War as the counter-part to Hot War. I don't think that's the right axis. I think it goes: Cold War - Hot War (i.e. Cold War is maneouvering and cats paw whilst avoiding provoking an all-out response, a Hot War is where real force is deployed to try and depose your enemy), and Shadow War - Open War (i.e. how much we try to conceal our actions vs. how much we no longer care). You can have a Cold Shadow War or a Hot Shadow War, or a Hot Open War. It's a 2x2 matrix.<br /> <br /> Vampires are obviously going to want their war to be a Shadow war as much as possible. But the more desperate they become, the more the temptation will be to discard secrecy where it's holding them back. It takes time to set up all the shell companies to hide your secret ownership of a dozen local businesses, it's not easy to recruit muscle when you're a faceless unknown in the shadows, infiltrating someone's secure haven in the day without attracting attention is more tricky than driving a JCB through their bedroom wall. A war can threaten the masquerade because going Open can give you powerful but dangerous advantages. It's a little like a game of brinkmanship - who dares drive closest to the edge? If you've ever seen the Netflix series Daredevil, the first season, recall Wilson Fisk's slow and steady manipulation in the shadows. And then (minor spoiler)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> how he out-maneouveres them with Vanessa's support and faith that others will see him as she does by suddenly going public and changing the game completely.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Imagine the way your players will reel if a vampire opponent, especially an elder, pulled that stunt on them half-way through a campaign just as they thought they were about to ferret said elder out into the sunlight. It wouldn't necessarily have to be a break in the Masquerade to be clear, anything along that theme.<br /> <br /> I hope some of this helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T01:02:03-07:00","id":977056,"title":"","content":"You also mention that it's Invictus vs. Circle of the Crone. These have quite different operating environments if we're going to be stereotypical. So they can target each other's &quot;habitats&quot; for want of a better term. For example, in the UK in the late Eighties, rumours of Satanic Ritual Abuse flew around the UK leading to children being separated from their families, paranoia, very dubious psychological assessments (for example, subjecting young children to leading questions inducing false memory syndrome). It was a Daily Mail style witchhunt. With influence in the media and police, Invictus could relatively easily stoke up such rumours in their area. The consequence would be the whole community on edge and keeping watch for strange meetings in the woods, children going missing, etc. Even people buying too many candles will attract attention if the community is scared enough. Invictus can hit the mattresses (Mafia term) whilst the Circle are forced to tip-toe around on edge the whole time because the city paper is running stories about peadophile satanists dancing naked in the woods. Just for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T05:17:44-07:00","id":978319,"title":"","content":"The game is set in NYC <br /> <br /> The Invictus are in Manhattan and the circle is in Queens. <br /> <br /> Right now the Circle has a lot of gargoyles protecting their area of influence. So Brooklyn has become a zone of contention between the Invictus and The Circle. <br /> <br /> The current prince of the Invictus is a kindred claims to have existed since the time of Alexander The Great. <br /> The Prince of the Circle has not only mastered blood sorcery but claims to have had a goddess known as the Blind Maiden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T15:38:57-07:00","id":978676,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine the Crones would find their mundane mortal cults infiltrated, and their members progressively killed off by overly aggressive NYPD cops. They'd likely also find that the Invictus in Manhattan had started using their significant contacts on Wall Street (aided by the dominate discipline) to buy up property used and owned by higher ups in the Circle.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I suspect the Crones would start searching for some type of apocalyptic level ritual which would allow them to significantly harm the Invictus from afar. I imagine they'd also find themselves kidnapping bankers and casting the Cheval ritual on them to spy on the Invictus. The Circle should essentially make it so that the Invictus doesn't feel comfortable meeting in large numbers or communicating too loudly. This would allow the Circle to pick off isolated members of the Invictus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5106-umoja","name":"Umoja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T04:27:12-07:00","id":978947,"title":"","content":"Where are the other coventants in this war? If say the Ordo Dracul and the Carthians side with the CoC and Lancea Sanctum with Invictus, that could change the balance of power.<br /> <br /> Otherwise Invictus would mostly manipulate mortal society, ghouls, and low level vampires against the CoC, but CoC would mostly use magical creatures, magic rites, and in some cases brute force to kill off Invictus and key pawns.<br /> <br /> So expect void creatures, blood gods, humuculus, gargoyles, zombies, undead animals hunting Invictus and they're agents, while the Invictus respond with mortal authories, and hit squads of vampires and ghouls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:31:18-07:00","id":979046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/976433-what-kind-of-signs-would-humans-notice-when-vampires-go-to-war-with-each-other?p=978947#post978947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are the other coventants in this war? If say the Ordo Dracul and the Carthians side with the CoC and Lancea Sanctum with Invictus, that could change the balance of power.<br /> <br /> Otherwise Invictus would mostly manipulate mortal society, ghouls, and low level vampires against the CoC, but CoC would mostly use magical creatures, magic rites, and in some cases brute force to kill off Invictus and key pawns.<br /> <br /> So expect void creatures, blood gods, humuculus, gargoyles, zombies, undead animals hunting Invictus and they're agents, while the Invictus respond with mortal authories, and hit squads of vampires and ghouls.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Currently the Ordo Dracul is currently held up on their island &quot;Staten Island&quot;, The Prince of the Ordo have said they have sided with the Invictus but have not sent any troops because they are worried the invictus might try and take their land also even though the invictus would have to be insane to try with how strange it is.<br /> <br /> The Carthian's and the Invictus have a tentative Alliance with small spats here or there. The Carthian's have a new leader currently due to an attack that happened on their power structure.<br /> <br /> Now the Lancea Sanctum are having real troubles. They had Brooklyn under their control till several attacks from an unknown group destroyed 80% of there power in the region now leader to other covenants wants their land. If that was not enough their prince was taken out. Unknown to them their God has now taken interest in their plight. A new Prince has taken control with what seems like the power of god behind him.<br /> <br /> If this was not enough with all the in fighting going on right across the water a unified Invictus wants all of New York and wants the complete destruction of all high ranking officials in the Manhattan invictus and the removal of all other covenants in NYC.<br /> <br /> The Invictus has things like mages on their side and other strange things. Also a very power General and a clever Judex on her side. Also Elders. <br /> <br /> The Ordo have some very strange horrors and worse under their control with a prince who seems to have mastered the unknown.<br /> <br /> The Circle has a Prince that has mastered Blood Magic to such a degree she can do spells that should take a few hours and a group almost reflexively it seems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","user":"Basic","date":". 09-30-2016, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}